<Base title="Teaching" description="Teaching operations, supply chain management and sustainability since 2007, from bachelor to executive programmes, plus doctoral training and mentoring.">
  <section class="view">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="mono">Teaching</span>
      <h1>Teaching</h1>
      <p class="lede">I've taught since 2007, to bachelor and master students, MBAs, PhD and DBA candidates and executives, mostly operations, supply chain management and sustainability. I try to bring research into the classroom through cases, simulations and real problems from companies.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cols2">
      <div class="block">
        <header><span class="mono">Where</span><h2>Programmes</h2></header>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li><span>2017–now</span><span>EADA Business School, Barcelona: master's, MBA, DBA and executive programmes</span></li>
          <li><span>2016–2017</span><span>Zaragoza Logistics Center (MIT-SCALE): PhD Summer Academy</span></li>
          <li><span>2014–2016</span><span>Audencia Nantes School of Management</span></li>
          <li><span>2007–2014</span><span>Politecnico di Milano: bachelor, master's and executive programmes in purchasing</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <header><span class="mono">With companies</span><h2>Custom programmes</h2></header>
        <p class="orgs">Since 2009 I have designed and taught custom programmes on purchasing and supply chain management for companies such as <b>IBM</b>, <b>Cisco Systems</b>, <b>Leonardo</b>, <b>UniCredit</b>, <b>Vodafone</b> and <b>Luxottica</b>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="block">
      <header><span class="mono">PhD and DBA candidates, young researchers</span><h2>Doctoral education</h2></header>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li><span>2026</span><span>Keynote at the IPSERA doctoral workshop on empirical research strategies in purchasing and supply management</span></li>
        <li><span>2025–now</span><span>Research methods course in the EADA Executive DBA</span></li>
        <li><span>2025–now</span><span>Mentor in the EurOMA mentorship programme and at the Academy of Management OSCM doctoral consortium</span></li>
        <li><span>2024–2025</span><span>EDEN doctoral seminar on sustainability in supply chains (EIASM), which I organised and taught at EADA</span></li>
        <li><span>2014–2019</span><span>Organiser of the IPSERA doctoral workshop, every year at the IPSERA conference</span></li>
        <li><span>2014–2017</span><span>Co-supervised two PhD theses at Politecnico di Milano; since then examiner or discussant of doctoral theses in Italy, the Netherlands, Spain, Sweden and the UK</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
